{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd","id":1478060,"title":"Dark Heroes in CoFD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-05T09:13:41-07:00","id":1478060,"title":"Dark Heroes in CoFD","content":"I've been trying to give Dark Heroes from Mirrors a homebrew update that would bring them into CoFD and also make them like other supernatural templates, and I need some help with it. So far, I've been working on the set of origins, which would be like clans from Vampire or Auspcies from Werewolf. Here's what I have so far:<br /> Descendants:<br /> These are the descendants of gods whether children or someone further down the line. Whether it be Zeus, Odin, or someone else, this is the source of their power. It can also be the sources of their strife if they\u2019re not careful. After all, enemies of their parents could be after them too.<br /> Examples: Heracles and the Volsungs.<br /> Starting Attribute: One of Resistance.<br /> Boon: Great Passions: Descendants feel emotions more strongly than normal humans do. They get to pick an emotion in addition to their virtue and vice. They can replenish a point of willpower per day if they get in a scene where they feel that emotion.<br /> Flaw: Weakness to Hubris: Descendants are particularly weak to Hubris. They take a -3 (maybe increase the penalty?) penalty to all rolls to resist losing Hubris.<br /> Stereotypes:<br /> Prodigies: It would seem that humanity has potential too. Good. We need sidekicks, after all.<br /> Incarnations: It\u2019s like looking in a mirror.<br /> Champions: Why doesn\u2019t dad love me like he loves you? And why do you have to be every bit as good as us? I\u2019d be more pissed if you weren\u2019t so awesome!<br /> <br /> Prodigies:<br /> These are people who have unlocked the inner potential of humanity. They have gained power most humans can\u2019t even dream of and look for the next step.<br /> Examples: Odysseus and Fionn mac Cumhaill.<br /> Starting Attribute: One of Power.<br /> Boon: Potential Unleashed: Prodigies spend 1 less experience point on skills (maybe attributes or something different?).<br /> Flaw: Origins in Humanity: The fact that Prodigies don\u2019t have a higher power as a source of their strength leaves them fundamentally human in some key ways. They get a point of health for every two levels of Arete instead of one.<br /> Stereotypes:<br /> Descendants: They\u2019re a bit arrogant, but if they have your back, you can count on them.<br /> Incarnations: You were a god in a past life? Damn.<br /> Champions: I feel sorry for them. They have the same power we do but must work for someone to get it.<br /> <br /> Incarnations:<br /> These are either gods that have incarnated in human form or ancient heroes who\u2019ve reincarnated into new bodies. They acquired the power of their predecessors and may even be able to unlock their memories.<br /> Examples: Most Hindu heroes.<br /> Starting Attribute: One of Finesse.<br /> Boon: This Seems Familiar. Choose someone you\u2019re the incarnation or reincarnation of. When you encounter a situation that is similar to something from a myth or legend involving your past self, a specific story, roll Intelligence+Wits. Each success adds to a dice pool that can be spent on any rolls in the scene. This ability can only be used once per scene and you can only use each die in the pool once.<br /> Flaw: Incarnations risk being overwhelmed by their memories. If they use the above boon more than twice a day, they must roll Resolve. A failure means the memories are too much for their brain to handle and they lose half the bonus they rolled and a point of Willpower. A dramatic failure also applies the stunned tilt.<br /> Stereotypes:<br /> Descendants: These guys get us.<br /> Prodigies: Normal mortals who\u2019ve reached supernatural levels of talent. Impressive.<br /> Champions: They are in service to someone. Let\u2019s hope it\u2019s someone friendly.<br /> <br /> Champions:<br /> A god, powerful spirit, or perhaps even an order has bestowed incredible power on these people. Their great power comes at its own cost, as they are beholden to whoever gave them this power in one way or another.<br /> Examples: King Arthur and David.<br /> Starting Attribute: One of Power.<br /> Boon: Blessed by Power: Once per day, Champions may call upon the power of whatever patron they have. This gives them bonus dice equal to their Arete for a single roll.<br /> Flaw: Required Obedience: Each session, the Storyteller gets a pool of dice equal to the Champion\u2019s Arete. If a champion does something their patron would not approve of or go against their orders, they may use some of that pool to reduce the Champion\u2019s own dice pool.<br /> Stereotypes:<br /> Descendants: They have a lot of bravado, but it\u2019s to cover up their daddy issues. Still, they have legitimate reasons for those. Give them your sympathy.<br /> Prodigies: They have more suspicion of non-humans than the rest of us. They might be the smartest of all.<br /> Incarnations: They have similar origins to the Descendants but none of the bravado. It\u2019s really weird.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Also, I need ideas for the fifth of these origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","user":"xela_nut","date":". 04-05-2022, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T09:57:40-07:00","id":1478067,"title":"","content":"Before I can say anything, I would need to know why you're adding an X-Splat to Dark Heroes, what they're supposed to do for the template, and how they're supposed to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T10:28:19-07:00","id":1478069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478067#post1478067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I can say anything, I would need to know why you're adding an X-Splat to Dark Heroes, what they're supposed to do for the template, and how they're supposed to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm putting in an X-Splat to make the Dark Heroes fit the normal Chronicles of Darkness format. This is to make them more fleshed-out than what they were in Mirrors. In terms of lore, the X-Splat describes the origins of the characters' powers. In terms of mechanics, the X-Splat is there to give the Dark Heroes both an extra advantage and an extra weakness depending on which the player chooses. I think how they describe how the characters got their powers is pretty obvious, and the way it's supposed to affect mechanics is by having the extra advantage and weakness balance each other out and not be overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","user":"xela_nut","date":".  Edit: Clarity 04-05-2022, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T16:51:19-07:00","id":1478101,"title":"","content":"I could\u2019ve sworn that there was a homebrew hack for Mage: The Ascension where the poster imported the concept of x-splats from CofD to its mages\u2026 but my search-fu doesn\u2019t turn up any. Gah. <br /> <br /> Anyways, here\u2019s what I remember of it so that you can use it for inspiration:<br /> <br /> <b>Wands</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via study. It could be the fruition of long years of passionate training, or a flash of genius that clicked after understanding the right piece of knowledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Cups</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via heritage. The lineage in question could be as weird as extradimensional aliens and shapeshifting dragons, or relatively mundane as royalty or a \u2018real-life\u2019 historical figure. <br /> <br /> <b>Swords</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via instrument. This is where you get the bearer of magic swords and forbidden grimoires, and the beneficiaries/victims of suspiciously high-spec cybernetic implants.<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacles</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via bargain. Maybe you made a deal with the Devil, or sealed a pact with the spirits, or swore to become a deity\u2019s champion, or took to heart someone\u2019s last wishes at their dying breath.<br /> <br /> <b>Jokers</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via sheer chance. Maybe you got struck by lightning, or bit by a radioactive spider. Or some god noticed you and decided you were worthy. Or some other sort of miscellany that also could fit into the other four splats if you looked at them the right way.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as I type the above, I see some resemblances to Deviant\u2019s Origins and Clades. You could look them over too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T04:47:28-07:00","id":1478199,"title":"","content":"Never heard of this, but it seems rather interesting. It also provides the key for a couple of rather interesting potential Story Hooks, such as a Descendant being literally, physically descended from the Dark Mother of B:tP, or an Incarnation being their namesake of Mother Luna or the God-Machine from W:tF and D:tD respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T05:50:00-07:00","id":1478201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478101#post1478101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could\u2019ve sworn that there was a homebrew hack for Mage: The Ascension where the poster imported the concept of x-splats from CofD to its mages\u2026 but my search-fu doesn\u2019t turn up any. Gah.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here\u2019s what I remember of it so that you can use it for inspiration:<br /> <br /> <b>Wands</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via study. It could be the fruition of long years of passionate training, or a flash of genius that clicked after understanding the right piece of knowledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Cups</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via heritage. The lineage in question could be as weird as extradimensional aliens and shapeshifting dragons, or relatively mundane as royalty or a \u2018real-life\u2019 historical figure.<br /> <br /> <b>Swords</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via instrument. This is where you get the bearer of magic swords and forbidden grimoires, and the beneficiaries/victims of suspiciously high-spec cybernetic implants.<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacles</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via bargain. Maybe you made a deal with the Devil, or sealed a pact with the spirits, or swore to become a deity\u2019s champion, or took to heart someone\u2019s last wishes at their dying breath.<br /> <br /> <b>Jokers</b> \u2014 Those who Awakened via sheer chance. Maybe you got struck by lightning, or bit by a radioactive spider. Or some god noticed you and decided you were worthy. Or some other sort of miscellany that also could fit into the other four splats if you looked at them the right way.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as I type the above, I see some resemblances to Deviant\u2019s Origins and Clades. You could look them over too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. That helps a lot. I think I might actually split Champions into two types. One will be the guys like David and Jason who are directly chosen by a deity, which will retain the champion name. The other will be more like King Arthur and will be people who got their powers from a magic item of some sort. I just need to come up with a name and mechanics for those guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","user":"xela_nut","date":". 04-07-2022, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T05:52:48-07:00","id":1478202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478199#post1478199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard of this, but it seems rather interesting. It also provides the key for a couple of rather interesting potential Story Hooks, such as a Descendant being literally, physically descended from the Dark Mother of B:tP, or an Incarnation being their namesake of Mother Luna or the God-Machine from W:tF and D:tD respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dark Heroes come from the Mirrors book. It's for 1E, but I'd highly recommend taking a look at it. It has a lot of stuff that's pretty good and applies regardless of edition. And those are pretty good ideas. Seeing a werewolf finding out that the person he's talking to is an incarnation of Luna would definitely be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T08:32:15-07:00","id":1478215,"title":"","content":"I'll have to double down on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>' questions.<br /> <br /> <b>Why</b> are you adding an X-Splat to Dark Heroes? Why do you so badly think they need it?<br /> <br /> <b>What</b> they're <i>conceptually</i> supposed to do for the template? Not what mechanics you'll put in, what they'll bring of interest to the table?<br /> <br /> <b>How</b> it's going to accomplish that? What type of rules and mechanics, which themes and moods, which options that don't exist otherwise?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, while <i>exploring</i> origins is interesting, making them into an X-Splat is completely unnecessary. Their RAW works fine with any origin whatsoever. Having an X-Splat just to make them look like other main splats isn't a good thing either, it creates the problem of going through a major work on rules without a clear picture of your goals just because you feel you have to. I see no problem at all with them being a simpler splat, I'm unconvinced that their concept needs this extra mechanical layer.<br /> <br /> Do you have a <u>pitch</u> for this that explores how those changes makes them more interesting and what concepts they'll bring or change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T11:11:56-07:00","id":1478226,"title":"","content":"Worth mentioning that there is already a 2E version of Dark Heroes as part of <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/323602/Mirrors-Dark-Antiquity\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Dark Antiquity</a>. I'd say it's worth a look, if only to avoid overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12220-dark-lord-potato","name":"Dark Lord Potato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T12:24:56-07:00","id":1478231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478069#post1478069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm putting in an X-Splat to make the Dark Heroes fit the normal Chronicles of Darkness format. This is to make them more fleshed-out than what they were in Mirrors. In terms of lore, the X-Splat describes the origins of the characters' powers. In terms of mechanics, the X-Splat is there to give the Dark Heroes both an extra advantage and an extra weakness depending on which the player chooses. I think how they describe how the characters got their powers is pretty obvious, and the way it's supposed to affect mechanics is by having the extra advantage and weakness balance each other out and not be overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>*rubs the bridge of her nose*<br /> *puts on her <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BMMGwtklEeE\" target=\"_blank\">choice of hubris-chasing protagonist song</a>*<br /> <br /> So, &quot; to make a thing fit the format&quot; is not just a bad argument in almost any creative venture and is how you end up with cliche riddled properties (and very bad Beast Y/Z-Splat conversations, but that's an unrelated gripe), It's also just not true for either major templates or major gamelines. Changeling has 6 X-Splats, Demon has 4, Beast and Deviant functionally have two different kinds of X-Splats, Hunter famously has none (a useful note on that later, though), and Dark Heroes aren't even the only major published template without splats at all, with the Purified from Immortals also not relying on the splat set up. Moving away from major templates, you can also construct Dark Heroes using a variety of options, including merit templates as seen in Hurt Locker (on record, this is probably what I would go to as a Second Edition incarnation for Dark Heroes), B-Splats, Merits, or just otherwise comprehensive lesser templates, all of which also do not rely on the X-Splat argument.<br /> <br /> I get wanting to to flesh them out, but it's got to be a purposeful direction, otherwise you start deviating away from their themes and ideas. As a quick and ready example, by putting an emphasis on their Origin, this presents a game where the protagonists have a particular relationship <i>to</i> that origin (look no further than Deviant literally demonstrating that fact)-which <i>can be interesting</i>, but you have to be sure that's what you want to do either in adjoinment to the splat's theme of Heroic Hubris.<br /> <br /> THe big thing is that Dark Heroes <i>work</i> for the context their presented in their context. They're a potent template, but they're not a <i>complicated </i>template. Asides from updating them to 2nd Edition, they work pretty fine. They don't worry about things like where they come from because they are people whose talents and skills make them an <i>honest to god</i> challenge for the powers of the world handle. Because so much of who they are depends on what they specifically do, boxing with conventional X-splats has the risk of <i>limiting</i> character creation-and because Heroes are modeled after lone world-changers, the conventional y-splat feels like it often gets in the way of how Dark Heroes are supposed to feel like their personal ambitions and investments are things which people gather around, and which other like people are often only to going to connect to on the band level and otherwise are likely to be such big personalities with impactful actions and decisions that it keeps Dark Heroes from developing conventional organizations or philosophies.<br /> <br /> Updating it means having an understanding of why things changed between editions and finding the right blend of keeping to that to bending the intent for Dark Heroes themes*. <i>Adding</i> something means making a decision of how much to try and keep to the original themes, moods, and atmospheres of the original versus how much to deviate from, and how much an addition does that.<br /> <br /> So I can give an example so I can sort of more readily demonstrate what I'm talking about it-so a fair while back I got the random urge to give Hunter, of all gamelines, an X-Splat-and I started that exercise with an acknowledgement of all the reasons why Hunter <i>didn't need</i> an X-Splat so I could be square in knowing why, what, and how I was doing <i>that exact thing</i>. In this case, I made the x-splat Wounds, broad categorizations of the sort of traumas that ignite the desperation that defines almost every hunter's Vigil, with the goal of it being an add-on that players or storyteller could apply to signal more personally driven, emotionally grounded stories that centers on the fact that most, if not all, hunters are damaged people with an unhealthy coping mechanism, and with that incentivize desperate action trying to prevent or avenge similar traumas while also creating conditions where coming across reminders of that trauma is spiralling, and point out how the desperation that comes with dealing with trauma parallels other supernatural instances**. And I did all of that because I felt like that was a viable and interesting thing that related to the themes and ideas of Hunter that I felt weren't as well expressed in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> And the thing of that is that while it's what I went with for that experiment, it's not the only way I could have gone. I noted, in my justification, that in first edtion for Hunter, the closest thing that that it had to an x-splat was the Professional Training merit, due to what was, at the time, an exclusive presence in that game line that gave direction on what your character, where they came from, and what they did. From that little notice, it's not hard to imagine Hunter having an X-Splat of Service, which would not only guarentee you dots in the Professional Training merit, but also offer ways in which you excel in situations where it lines up, offers benefits for creatively reapplying those skills and expectations, and pointing out ways that training trips up hunters. Not only is that just as rooted in what Hunter has done before, but it also anchors it in the working class mentality that first edition was largely grounded in, really bringing in how the everyman can step up to the shadows and make their difference, but also comment on how the modern world and that very same mentality contributes to the deliberate non-focus on the shadows in the first place.<br /> <br /> And both of those are motivated by not just wanting to create a X-splat for Hunter just because, but by taking portions of Hunters text and creating an alternative play style that emphasizes certain themes and ideas in Hunter to create a more distinctive style of play-and mind you, those <i>are</i> alternatives, because I basically have no good argument that Hunter <i>should</i> have an X-Splat, because no, they don't.<br /> <br /> ANYWAYS.<br /> <br /> If you're really dedicated to the idea of an X-Splat, and assumedly an adjacent y-splat, then I would probably start around the idea of heroic archetype and common cause to commit hubris over, to help players focus on what sort of character they want to be <i>in play</i>, and with that stated, I might recommend looking over at how Mage does things for ideas (in fact, while I wouldn't suggest making Dark Heroes Supernally-powered, a lazy part of me actually kind of groks the idea that Dark Heroes are <i>also</i> in the Orders), and I would also point at Beast's Hungers for ways to think on more directed hubris-but again, I would <b><i>really</i></b> start on interrogating on what you think a fleshed out Dark Hero splat should be like, and what any planned additions would <i>actually</i> contribute to that ideal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Lord Potato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478226#post1478226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth mentioning that there is already a 2E version of Dark Heroes as part of <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/323602/Mirrors-Dark-Antiquity\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Dark Antiquity</a>. I'd say it's worth a look, if only to avoid overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, overlap with another fan project is the last thing I'd be worried about, even if it's a fan project on the STV.<br /> <br /> *for example, the Rapidity Mastery was broken in 1st Edtion, but so was any combat technique that had multiple moves, so was more tolerable-but 2nd Edition made those a lot more restricted and generally opted to create &quot;flurry&quot; style moves where so long as a character was commited to a thing(usually violence), they could have a state that basicially automatically added a success so long as it was applicable (stay in a swordmaster's reach and you take a damage each turn in addition to attacks, again as conventional)-but I guarentee you anyone remembering Dark Heroes remember and probably want some form of Rapidity, so for that you need to answer-do you adapt that as a Flurry style thing, do you break convention with 2nd Edition and keep it the same to emphasize the particular excellence Dark Heroes can get up to, or do you find a middle ground, possibly turning it into a carry forward bonus if you hit or a recovery bonus if you fail, or turning it into a multiple target applying thing, letting you do a small autofire burst in combat or letting you handle two locks or computer programs at once? Stuff like that is the thought for updating.<br /> **In a section that explores Slasher-Beast connections to hunters and trauma and how, with resonance and all matters of other metaphysics, to get all Annihilation metaphor-y with trauma, we have some supernatural merits associated with the Wounds-I bring this up to just say that I'm very happy with one merit name, being &quot;The World Goes Dark.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-07-2022, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T12:27:34-07:00","id":1478232,"title":"","content":"Let's call this a double post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T13:37:56-07:00","id":1478234,"title":"","content":"Okay, first off, thank you to everyone who's posted on this thread so far. You've all helped me a lot, and I'm hoping that I understand what you're saying. So, to answer a few questions:<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> , I am not dedicated to the idea of making an X-Splat. I thought that would be a good way to start, and you have a point that it might not need an update, so I'll rethink the x-splat thing in general. It also seems that I should have been thinking of the themes before the mechanics and not the other way around. I don't necessarily want to limit the player options either.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> , I don't think I can answer all your questions, which is part of the problem that I had in the first place, but they gave me a general idea of what I want to do that I'll tell everyone now.<br /> It might be a bit too ambitious, so let me know what you think. I'm presenting my logic pure and simple, and I am more than willing to remove things if you think I'm trying to handle too much or the themes won't work.<br /> <br /> Basically, to put it in terms of other games, it's sort of a mixture of Mage and Deviant in terms of its themes.<br /> On the mage end, the idea is that the dark heroes are all people ascending to a high level of power and possible divinity; however, they must deal with their own hubris in the process. Here I'm drawing a bit on Werewolf's version of Integrity. Basically, the idea is that if hubris gets too high, they'll think of themselves too highly and it'll make them suffer in some way. But if hubris gets too low, they'll risk suffering by giving up on everything because they'll lose hope. The idea is still in its infancy and I'm not sure if that's the best way to go about it or what the exact mechanical effects would be.<br /> <br /> On the sort of Deviant end, the reason why I thought an X-Splat would be a good idea (which I'm now reconsidering) is because I thought dark heroes having to deal with their origins was part of the whole mythos of mythical heroes in general. For example, let's say you have a dark hero who is the result of human potential coming forth. From their perspective, they might have earned their powers while other people just got lucky. Or they might feel inadequate because their origins are in humanity while dealing with other beings that may have been born supernatural. Both those could affect hubris, and an X-Splat may or may not be the best way to go about it. I'm not certain.<br /> <br /> Once more, thank you for commenting here, and I'm sorry if I'm a bit dense here. This is the first time I'm doing this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","user":"xela_nut","date":".  Edited for clarity 04-07-2022, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T00:23:44-07:00","id":1478263,"title":"","content":"Also uh sorry to ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, but where can I find your Wounds X-splat for Hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T02:35:56-07:00","id":1478268,"title":"","content":"Off-handed suggestion: You could also look to the Fae-Touched in Changeling 2E for inspiration. All of them got to where they are by making a promise, and they get a +1 to any action that asserts that promise\u2026 but the categories of promises are not handled as innate template features (such as splats), but Merits they can opt in and buy, and it\u2019s those Merits that give a mechanical oomph. Allows for more customizability this way, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T06:18:51-07:00","id":1478277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478268#post1478268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off-handed suggestion: You could also look to the Fae-Touched in Changeling 2E for inspiration. All of them got to where they are by making a promise, and they get a +1 to any action that asserts that promise\u2026 but the categories of promises are not handled as innate template features (such as splats), but Merits they can opt in and buy, and it\u2019s those Merits that give a mechanical oomph. Allows for more customizability this way, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a pretty good idea. All the heroes could have access to optional merits to represent certain things. Maybe they could have merits for their origins, or some non-merit trait that isn't required like an X-Splat is. The players could decide to ignore the origin thing if they want and, otherwise, they can take that trait or merit. Does that sound good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T15:23:39-07:00","id":1478302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478277#post1478277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a pretty good idea. All the heroes could have access to optional merits to represent certain things. Maybe they could have merits for their origins, or some non-merit trait that isn't required like an X-Splat is. The players could decide to ignore the origin thing if they want and, otherwise, they can take that trait or merit. Does that sound good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds simple and good enough to me, but dunno about others!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T17:24:46-07:00","id":1478308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478277#post1478277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty good idea. All the heroes could have access to optional merits to represent certain things. Maybe they could have merits for their origins, or some non-merit trait that isn't required like an X-Splat is. The players could decide to ignore the origin thing if they want and, otherwise, they can take that trait or merit. Does that sound good?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think that the concepts you're starting to flesh out now are interesting as a startinh point, and this idea of an optional trait for those things may work pretty well for Dark Heroes, each one deciding what is important in their Journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T23:22:07-07:00","id":1478325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478263#post1478263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also uh sorry to ask <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, but where can I find your Wounds X-splat for Hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once I'm satisfied with it, it's going on the STV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T01:53:22-07:00","id":1478339,"title":"","content":"Ohhh, I see. I wish you luck with that project of yours Arcane!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T07:26:32-07:00","id":1478357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478308#post1478308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that the concepts you're starting to flesh out now are interesting as a startinh point, and this idea of an optional trait for those things may work pretty well for Dark Heroes, each one deciding what is important in their Journey.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, so to expand on that idea, there are two options. One is it being a somewhat normal trait that's optional and the other being a merit. These traits or merits could be expanded upon to include more things than just origins, but I'll just stick to the child of a god thing for now to make figuring out the basics simple.<br /> <br /> It it was an optional trait, perhaps it would be in addition to or replacing the virtue or vice? If that's the case, then it might work like the Virtuous merit and be worth two dots:<br /> Child of a God: Regain willpower whenever your divine heritage causes you trouble. Example: Being attacked by werewolves or spirits because you're a child of Luna.<br /> <br /> But if it's a different trait, it might not be connected to Willpower. It might be more on the side of giving a bonus or penalty to something. I'm not certain about that.<br /> <br /> If it's a straight merit, it would probably be a 1 to 5 dot merit resembling a Hunter group or Professional Training or something. It might go something like:<br /> 1: You are the child of a god. Based on what type of god your parent is, you get the Unseen Sense merit related to them for free. (like werewolves for Luna, nature spirits for Demeter, or various other examples depending on what the players want).<br /> 2: As your connection expands, you get a free skill speciality in something related to your parent.<br /> 3: Maybe 9-Again rolls to one skill at that point?<br /> 4: Probably some supernatural ability or something else. Not sure about this and five.<br /> 5:<br /> <br /> So, any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T11:25:53-07:00","id":1478397,"title":"","content":"First you should flesh out a little more the basics, what are the themes yyou're going for. That's because later the best way to evaluate a mechanic will be to consider how it is working in relation to its goal.<br /> <br /> So, are you set on working with the theme of heroic hubris and disconnection? What that should mean in the game? And how it differ from other games with similar themes, like Mage?<br /> <br /> I think this is a good direction, it just needs some more work. There's a lot of ways of exploring such themes without stepping on other games, but since it's your child, you need to decide what you want to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:11:29-07:00","id":1478411,"title":"","content":"I agree with monteparnas, focus on the basics before everything else. A house cannot stand for long without a properly built physical foundation, and it is much the same elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T23:36:31-07:00","id":1478472,"title":"","content":"Again, deeply interrogate what's going on with Dark Heroes, and what you want it to do <i>well</i>. From there, what feels like organic extensions of that, what feels like missing teeth, and so forth.<br /> <br /> If I have some time, I'll see if I can come up with some places I would start any sort of rebuild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T06:36:40-07:00","id":1478488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478060-dark-heroes-in-cofd?p=1478472#post1478472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, deeply interrogate what's going on with Dark Heroes, and what you want it to do <i>well</i>. From there, what feels like organic extensions of that, what feels like missing teeth, and so forth.<br /> <br /> If I have some time, I'll see if I can come up with some places I would start any sort of rebuild.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that'll help a lot. And thanks to everyone else who commented on this so far. So, in regards to your thoughts on the what's going on and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25791\" data-vbnamecard=\"25791\">TerrorCooper</a> 's suggestions on the themes, here's what I have so far:<br /> <br /> Heroic Hubris:<br /> This is similar to mage, but it's a bit different as well. This form of hubris is more based around overconfidence. As in, dark heroes risk thinking they're better than everyone else and taking on more than they can handle. Rather than doing something like becoming abusive to mortals, a hero with hubris might try to attack a pack of werewolves with a butter knife to use an extreme example. And if I end up going with dark heroes gradually becoming god-like beings as their power increases, they might try to ascend too soon and suffer what Bellerophon did.<br /> And please let me know if this is too similar to mage and I should alter it further. I don't know all that much about mage compared to other gamelines, and I'm worried that I'm going too close to their form of hubris.<br /> <br /> Where you come from:<br /> You come from somewhere, whether that's a group of mortals, a house of dark heroes, the servants of a vampire or something else. Where you come from affects your life, whether you want it to or not and even if you have no idea where you come from. To give an in-game example, if your dark hero is a child of Luna, they might get attacked or enlisted to aid werewolves or spirits even if they don't know why. Though, once again, this isn't necessarily the biggest theme compared to others.<br /> <br /> The respect of heroes:<br /> Essentially, heroes try to curb their hubris with respect. Even if they hate someone, they still try to treat them with respect because hubris might take hold otherwise. And heroes love it when they find someone they can genuinely respect. But this is a very difficult thing because there are some beings out there that deserve no respect, and dark heroes know it while also knowing that disrespect can lead them down the dark road to hubris.<br /> <br /> So, any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}